+Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: a single transparent PNG brush-stroke background for an existing newspaper UI link. Input image 1 is a visual reference for the exact brush gesture, its broad horizontal sweep, a few bold diagonal back-and-forth bends, tapered beginning and end, and naturally frayed dry-marker edges. Create one ORIGINAL hand-drawn zigzag brush swash closely following that reference's gesture: long skinny lead-in on the left, then only three or four broad, loose diagonal sweeps across the width, loose rounded turn-backs with changing pressure and overlap, ending with a tapered flick at the right. It should look like a real human quickly marked it with a thick felt-tip marker, with rough bristle edges, a few dry ink gaps and tiny edge flecks. Use muted warm golden yellow marker ink (#E4BD43), with an otherwise completely transparent background. Wide horizontal canvas, approximately 4.2:1 aspect, stroke fills about 92% of the width and 75% of the height with clear margins, viewed flat from directly above. This will go BEHIND separately rendered dark 'Race track' lettering, so generate NO TEXT, NO LETTERS, NO LOGO, NO FRAME, NO PAPER, NO SHADOW, NO GRADIENT. Do not make a regular triangular waveform or repeating vertical hatching. Preserve genuine transparent alpha; no white background or baked checkerboard.
